WEBVTT

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.628
...and since I was
the only crew member

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.195
who could survive
the corrosive atmosphere,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.764
it was up to me
to retrieve the data module

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.310
and save the day.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.077
Ah, here I am...

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.706
mission accomplished.

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.807
Ah...

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.579
Then, of course there was

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.483
the perilous mission
to La'voti V.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.317
You remember that one,
don't you, Mr. Paris?

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.756
How could I forget?

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:29.386
Here you are
after your unfortunate slip

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.659
into the fetid mud pits
of Pala Mar.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.298
Hey, I was pushed.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.357
Of course you were.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.835
Thank you, Doctor.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.838
We've all enjoyed
your holo-images enormously.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.567
Oh, but I haven't
finished yet.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.733
There's more?

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.969
The best is yet to come,
Lieutenant.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.102
I've created a fascinating

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.115
12-part holographic essay
which I call "Under the Skin:

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.117
Humanoid Anatomy as Art."

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.382
Let's begin
with this stunning magnification

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.980
of the Vulcan
reproductive gland.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.117
Note the composition.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.162
The subtle variations in color.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.932
2100 hours, Commander.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.534
All systems reporting normal.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.159
Acknowledged.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:14.697
Like I said, it's 2100 hours.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.105
I heard you the first time,
Harry.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.701
They've been in there
over an hour.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.939
I'm aware of that.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.606
Didn't the Captain ask you
to rescue them after 30 minutes?

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.651
Harry, you and I
were lucky enough

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.414
to enjoy the Doctor's
scintillating exhibition

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.955
for two full hours.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.457
Would it really be fair of us
to deny our friends

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.186
the same
unforgettable experience?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.728
Of course not, sir.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:43.127
Thank you.
Thank you for coming.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.898
We'll do it again soon.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.134
We've still got thousands
of light-years to while away.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.903
This could be a weekly event.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.910
What happened to going
to Yellow Alert

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.967
after half an hour?

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.343
Commander Chakotay appears to
have disobeyed a direct order.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.315
Definitely grounds
for court-martial.

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.715
Hey, Neelix.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.721
Coffee?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.417
I could use a whole pot.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.925
Let me guess.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:11.123
The Doctor's photographic essay?

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.926
One mind-numbing image
after the next.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.296
Oh, I don't know.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.733
I thought some of those pictures
were pretty funny.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.431
You mean like the one where Tom
slipped into a mud pit?

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.772
You're famous.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.308
Then, of course, there's the one

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.934
depicting
a certain Chief Engineer

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.945
with her foot stuck
in a plasma injector.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.105
What?

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.274
Really? Well, I seem
to have missed that one.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.614
The Doctor must have taken it
out of the exhibition.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.346
Oh, I can't wait to
get my hands on it.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.945
Maybe I can distribute it
to everyone's personal database.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.650
Try it and I'll kill you...

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.752
right after I finish deleting
the Doctor's program.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.855
What'd you put
in this coffee, Neelix?

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.365
I'm reading
a massive energy wave

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.268
900,000 kilometers
off the starboard bow,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.306
heading right for us.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:55.466
Source?

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.634
Unknown.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.108
Shields up.
Evasive maneuvers.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.776
The wave just changed course.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.144
It seems to be tracking us!

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.182
Go to warp 8.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.910
Too late.
Engines are down.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.541
Everybody hang on.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.331
All stop.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.337
Shields are holding.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.897
Minor damage to the hull plating
on Deck 15.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:09.906
No injuries.

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.374
Stand down Red Alert.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.469
Captain, when the wave hit,

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.514
our communications array
received a download.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.912
What sort of download?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.483
I'm not sure.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.813
Lots of information.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.354
I can't decipher it,
but there's an audio component.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.117
Let's hear it.

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:35.760
Harry, try all the standard
decryption algorithms.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.268
It's strange.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.668
The wave followed us,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.070
but it didn't cause any damage.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.474
Instead, we get a download
to our database.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.342
I'd say it's a pretty good bet

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.381
somebody's trying
to tell us something.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.781
The wave left
a residual ion trail.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.944
We might be able
to locate its point of origin.

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.850
Set a course.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.631
Looks like it's taken
quite a beating.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.695
Life signs?

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.207
One. Nonhumanoid.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.674
It's very faint.

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:18.711
Probably injured.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.109
Beam it to Sick Bay.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.612
Are you sure that's wise,
Captain?

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:23.273
I'm betting
that message we received

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:24.714
was some sort of distress call

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:27.844
and if we're going to help,
I'd rather do it on Voyager.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.578
The physiology is so unusual

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.124
the tricorder can't make heads
or tails of it.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.887
The creature's
obviously injured,

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.895
but I haven't a clue
how to treat it

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.430
or even diagnose it.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:41.296
My scans came up with something
interesting, Captain.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.198
The interfaces
on the alien's vessel

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:45.760
can only be activated
chemically.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.533
I'm guessing that this life-form

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.939
somehow interfaces directly
with the ship's systems

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.943
using biochemical secretions
to give commands.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.173
That would explain
how it can fly a ship.

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:56.738
I'm hoping this can
also help us figure out...

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.084
No! You'll hurt B'Elanna!

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.556
Get it off of me!

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:07.388
Janeway to Kim.
Beam the alien life-form

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.020
back to its vessel now!

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.859
I'm having trouble
getting a lock.

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.729
It's piercing her neck!

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:21.568
Her heart and lungs
are seriously compromised

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.233
and her kidneys are failing.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.539
The creature's also secreting
some kind of paralyzing agent

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.737
into her bloodstream.

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.178
How do we get it off her?

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:29.407
I can't remove it surgically,

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:30.915
not without doing
irreparable harm

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.142
to B'Elanna's internal organs.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:33.742
Can we get a lock
on the creature...

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.752
transport it off?

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:35.913
Not unless we want to beam

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.115
B'Elanna's cardiopulmonary
system along with it.

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.556
We have to do something!

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.354
No one is disputing
that, Mr. Paris.

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:42.860
The question is: What?

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:45.261
If I'm to have any hope
of devising a treatment,

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.424
I'll need to brush up
on my exobiology.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.468
What do you mean, "brush up"?

00:07:49.535 --> 00:07:51.765
Don't you have all this
information in your database?

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:54.033
I may be a walking
medical encyclopedia,

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.937
but even I don't know
everything.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:57.703
My matrix simply isn't
large enough.

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:59.438
Maybe we can do
better than giving you

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.774
a crash course in exobiology.

00:08:00.847 --> 00:08:02.872
Maybe we can provide
you with a consultant.

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.244
I'd be delighted, but how?

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:07.343
By isolating the computer's
exobiology data files

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.446
and merging them
into an interactive matrix.

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:11.888
- A hologram.
- Exactly.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.548
That may not be
as simple as it sounds.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.890
It would need to be nearly
as sophisticated as I am...

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.987
tactile interfaces,
personality subroutines...

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:19.395
Harry could do it.

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.695
Search the database
for a leading exobiologist.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:22.893
If you want to add
a personality,

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:24.492
it may as well be based
on a real person.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.299
I'll have Harry meet you
on Holodeck 2.

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:28.431
Stay with her
and monitor her vital signs.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:29.839
Call me if there's any change.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.878
I still have my doubts
about this, Doc.

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.475
It's one thing
to create a simple hologram,

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.781
but you're trying to merge

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:44.118
an extensive database
with an interactive matrix.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.623
Don't be a pessimist, Mr. Kim.

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:46.885
Together, we'll create

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:48.790
a masterpiece
of holographic art.

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:50.795
A subject
for your next slide show?

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.091
- Perhaps.
- Can't wait.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.689
What's the name of that
exobiologist you chose?

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.792
Crell Moset.

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:58.234
Here's the file.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.864
Let's start with the parameters
for physical appearance.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.103
Computer, display
a holographic simulation

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.643
of Crell Moset.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.513
Have you mentioned
to anyone else

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:10.879
that this guy's a Cardassian?

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.248
What difference does it make?

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:14.581
Maybe you haven't heard.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:15.586
They're not the exactly

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:16.883
the friendliest folks
in the galaxy.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:18.548
I don't care
if he's the nastiest man

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:21.149
who ever lived, as long as he
can help us save B'Elanna.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.353
Good point.

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:25.522
Computer, transfer
all referenced medical files

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:27.156
to the simulation.

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.666
Transfer complete.

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:31.032
Now install
personality subroutines

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.697
and voice approximation.

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:35.331
Installation complete.

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:40.703
Dr. Moset, I'd like
to consult with you

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.111
about an alien life-form.

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:44.706
I am Crell Moset,

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:47.378
Chief Exobiology Specialist
Cardassia Prime,

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:49.717
...to perform
all surgical procedures.

00:09:49.789 --> 00:09:51.689
This is going well.
What's wrong?

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.225
Some sort of overload
in the interactive matrix.

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:56.124
Can you clear it up?

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:57.287
I'm trying.

00:09:57.363 --> 00:10:00.696
Computer, install
a recursive algorithm.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:03.360
Algorithm installed.

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:05.233
Try it again.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:06.703
Dr. Moset?

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:10.173
My friends call me Crell.

00:10:19.785 --> 00:10:21.776
It's a pleasure to meet you,
Crell.

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:23.822
And you, good man,
what's your name?

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:28.155
Actually, I'm in between
names at the moment.

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:30.161
I'm an Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:31.696
Interesting.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.425
But his friends call him Doc.

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:35.899
Aha. May I presume?

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:37.333
Certainly.

00:10:37.403 --> 00:10:40.304
So, Doc, how can
an old surgeon like me

00:10:40.373 --> 00:10:43.308
help a technological marvel
such as yourself?

00:10:43.376 --> 00:10:44.968
Oh, well...

00:10:45.111 --> 00:10:47.409
I've got a patient
with a rather unusual problem.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.506
She's become fused
with a nonhumanoid life-form

00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:51.777
I know nothing about.

00:10:51.851 --> 00:10:53.716
Nonhumanoid exobiology

00:10:53.786 --> 00:10:55.515
happens to be one
of my specialties.

00:10:55.588 --> 00:10:57.681
That's exactly why we've
created your program.

00:10:57.757 --> 00:10:58.849
Program?

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:00.414
You're a hologram as well.

00:11:00.493 --> 00:11:02.654
Interesting.

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:04.889
I'd like to see the patient
right away.

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.363
Mr. Kim, would you
do the honors, please?

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:07.865
No problem.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.924
Listen,
if he destabilizes again,

00:11:10.036 --> 00:11:11.663
take him off-line and call me.

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:12.795
Understood.

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:19.106
Lieutenant,
may I present Crell Moset?

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:20.406
It's a pleasure.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.879
She's been drifting
in and out of consciousness.

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:24.848
Don't be rude, Lieutenant.

00:11:24.917 --> 00:11:25.884
To him?

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:28.442
No offense, Doc,
but he's just a...

00:11:28.521 --> 00:11:30.819
A brilliant scientist
who's here to help us.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:32.323
This way, Crell.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.757
Hmm... I can see
why you're having difficulty.

00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:36.351
Its physiology doesn't match

00:11:36.429 --> 00:11:39.091
any of the standard
templates in our database.

00:11:39.165 --> 00:11:41.963
My guess would be
a cytoplasmic life-form.

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:44.195
I agree.
And from what I can tell,

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.465
it has co-opted
her vital systems.

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:47.699
She's Klingon...

00:11:47.773 --> 00:11:50.742
No, the cranial ridges
are less pronounced.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:51.970
Klingon-human hybrid.

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:52.975
Exactly.

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:54.374
Let's hope your instincts

00:11:54.447 --> 00:11:56.574
about the creature
are equally insightful.

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:57.616
I'm afraid

00:11:57.683 --> 00:11:59.617
this one is going
to require more

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:01.243
than a visual assessment.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.288
You have
an isomolecular scanner.

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:06.051
No. Just a standard issue
Starfleet tricorder.

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:09.788
No wonder you're having problems
making an accurate diagnosis.

00:12:09.862 --> 00:12:12.330
I suggested an upgrade
to the Starfleet people

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:13.922
at a joint medical conference,

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:17.833
but they assumed I was
just an arrogant Cardassian

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:20.565
trying to prove
his superiority...

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:22.766
or maybe they thought
I was a spy.

00:12:22.842 --> 00:12:24.935
I hope you weren't too offended.

00:12:25.044 --> 00:12:27.308
It's an unfortunate reality.

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:31.440
Sometimes even enlightened
races can't find common ground.

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:37.547
I may be able
to recalibrate this thing.

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:39.523
There. That should help.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.361
Amazing.

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:50.835
Well, someone from Starfleet
appreciates me.

00:12:52.872 --> 00:12:55.136
I've instructed the computer
to assign symbols

00:12:55.207 --> 00:12:57.573
to all the tones received
in the transmission.

00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:01.840
Looks like there were over
10,000 separate sounds

00:13:01.914 --> 00:13:03.313
used in this section
of the message.

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:05.247
It's going to be
a tough code to crack.

00:13:05.317 --> 00:13:06.443
Maybe we can get a little help

00:13:06.519 --> 00:13:07.918
from the alien vessel's
data banks.

00:13:07.987 --> 00:13:08.919
Good idea.

00:13:09.021 --> 00:13:09.919
Janeway to Seven of Nine.

00:13:10.022 --> 00:13:10.920
Yes.

00:13:11.056 --> 00:13:13.388
Any chance of downloading
the alien's data banks?

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:14.426
We're looking for anything

00:13:14.493 --> 00:13:15.926
that might help us
understand their language.

00:13:16.028 --> 00:13:18.087
We don't know how much time
B'Elanna has left.

00:13:18.164 --> 00:13:20.132
We must move quickly.

00:13:20.199 --> 00:13:22.690
The vessel is on the verge
of a complete systems failure.

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.326
Prepare to download the data.

00:13:24.403 --> 00:13:25.870
I heard the Captain.

00:13:27.006 --> 00:13:28.405
Is there a problem?

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:29.600
No. No problem.

00:13:29.675 --> 00:13:32.200
You seem uncomfortable
taking orders from me.

00:13:32.278 --> 00:13:33.768
It's just that I'm
used to taking orders

00:13:33.846 --> 00:13:34.778
from B'Elanna, that's all

00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:36.439
and to tell you the truth,
she doesn't...

00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:37.948
Doesn't like me.
Yes, I am aware of that.

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:39.482
However, the Captain
left me in charge

00:13:39.552 --> 00:13:41.611
during Lieutenant Torres'
absence.

00:13:41.687 --> 00:13:43.518
Her feelings about me
are irrelevant.

00:13:43.589 --> 00:13:45.614
Activate the interface
transceiver.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:47.886
Begin the download.

00:13:48.961 --> 00:13:50.952
I'm picking up a fluctuation

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.964
in the alien ship's
power source.

00:13:53.098 --> 00:13:55.794
It's disrupting
the interface transceiver.

00:13:55.868 --> 00:13:56.800
Reinitialize.

00:13:56.869 --> 00:13:58.200
I'm working on it.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.932
Its systems are overloading.

00:14:01.006 --> 00:14:02.439
Red Alert.

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:03.907
Engineering to Bridge.

00:14:04.009 --> 00:14:06.000
The alien vessel
is destabilizing.

00:14:06.078 --> 00:14:07.909
Its destruction is imminent.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:09.914
Can you download
the information first?

00:14:09.982 --> 00:14:11.779
We're trying.

00:14:11.851 --> 00:14:13.785
Captain, it's going to explode.

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:15.150
Ensign, back us off.

00:14:25.297 --> 00:14:26.924
What do we know so far?

00:14:27.032 --> 00:14:29.227
The life-form has taken
control of her body

00:14:29.301 --> 00:14:30.598
at the autonomic level,

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.569
drawing proteins
from her tissues,

00:14:32.638 --> 00:14:34.435
white blood cells
from her arteries.

00:14:34.506 --> 00:14:36.371
Which can be interpreted
in several ways.

00:14:36.442 --> 00:14:37.568
A form of attack.

00:14:37.643 --> 00:14:39.042
I find it odd

00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:41.477
that a species would evolve
an attack mechanism

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:43.412
that would leave it
so vulnerable.

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:46.383
Why not do its damage
and retreat?

00:14:46.452 --> 00:14:47.783
A parasite perhaps?

00:14:47.853 --> 00:14:49.218
Yes, I think so,

00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:51.848
but not any ordinary variety.

00:14:51.924 --> 00:14:55.087
It's unlikely it could
sustain itself like this

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.787
over the long term.

00:14:56.862 --> 00:14:58.261
Its own systems are damaged.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:02.198
It's doing this as a stopgap
measure to keep itself alive.

00:15:02.268 --> 00:15:05.101
So the patient's heart,
lungs, kidneys...

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.469
they're all augmenting
the alien's damaged system.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.235
It's using B'Elanna
as a life preserver.

00:15:10.309 --> 00:15:13.039
But if it needs her to survive,

00:15:13.112 --> 00:15:16.275
it's not about to let go
without a fight.

00:15:16.348 --> 00:15:18.612
I'd like to think that's a fight
you and I can win.

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:20.652
We do work well together.

00:15:20.719 --> 00:15:25.247
I just wish we had access
to my laboratory.

00:15:25.324 --> 00:15:29.488
It has all the instrumentation
we would need.

00:15:29.561 --> 00:15:31.153
Well, we'll just
have to improvise.

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:32.424
Not necessarily.

00:15:32.498 --> 00:15:35.228
We may be able to create
a reasonable facsimile

00:15:35.301 --> 00:15:36.928
of your laboratory
in our holodeck...

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.060
providing, of course,

00:15:38.137 --> 00:15:39.399
you can give
an accurate description.

00:15:39.471 --> 00:15:42.338
Oh, down to the smallest detail.

00:15:42.408 --> 00:15:46.868
It's more of a home to me
than... than my home.

00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:56.150
Tom.

00:15:58.724 --> 00:16:00.351
Hey, there.

00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:03.720
I can't move.

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:06.321
I know.

00:16:06.398 --> 00:16:07.387
But don't worry.

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:09.331
We'll get this thing off you.

00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:11.425
Just think.

00:16:11.503 --> 00:16:13.801
I could force you to listen
to rock 'n' roll all day

00:16:13.872 --> 00:16:16.102
and you wouldn't be able
to do a thing about it.

00:16:18.577 --> 00:16:20.044
Who is that?

00:16:20.112 --> 00:16:21.204
Relax.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.907
He's just a hologram...

00:16:23.015 --> 00:16:25.245
a specialist in exobiology.

00:16:25.317 --> 00:16:28.616
The Doc thinks he might be able
to help you.

00:16:28.687 --> 00:16:30.712
Can't he find somebody else?

00:16:30.789 --> 00:16:33.587
Apparently, this guy's the best.

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:36.924
Besides, he's just
a walking database.

00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:42.059
Hologram or not,
he's Cardassian.

00:16:42.134 --> 00:16:43.362
As far as I'm concerned,

00:16:43.435 --> 00:16:45.232
they're all
cold-blooded killers.

00:16:45.304 --> 00:16:48.296
I understand how you feel.

00:16:48.374 --> 00:16:51.104
Unfortunately,
that cold-blooded killer

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:54.270
may be the only one
who can save your life.

00:17:05.591 --> 00:17:06.523
Impressive.

00:17:06.592 --> 00:17:07.889
Mm.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.121
Is this where you did your work
on the Fostossa virus?

00:17:10.195 --> 00:17:13.062
No. Actually, I was

00:17:13.132 --> 00:17:16.898
on Bajor at the time,
during the occupation.

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:20.028
A sad chapter
in Cardassian history.

00:17:20.105 --> 00:17:22.471
We had no business being there,

00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:25.669
but try telling that
to the politicians.

00:17:25.744 --> 00:17:28.907
When I think of the resources
that were squandered,

00:17:29.014 --> 00:17:31.505
the lives that were lost...

00:17:31.583 --> 00:17:34.381
From what I understand,
you saved thousands of lives.

00:17:34.453 --> 00:17:38.048
In retrospect, I don't know how.

00:17:38.123 --> 00:17:40.023
The military had
everything they needed,

00:17:40.092 --> 00:17:41.423
but the civilian hospitals?

00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:43.927
No staff,
the crudest equipment...

00:17:43.996 --> 00:17:44.928
Don't tell me.

00:17:44.997 --> 00:17:46.191
You were forced to improvise.

00:17:46.265 --> 00:17:47.254
Yes!

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:48.264
I know what that's like.

00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:49.425
I didn't have the resources

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:52.664
to try traditional methods,
so I experimented

00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:56.834
with procedures that never
would have occurred to me

00:17:56.909 --> 00:17:58.638
under ordinary circumstances.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:03.238
The discovery of the cure was
almost accidental, really.

00:18:03.315 --> 00:18:04.339
You're being modest, Crell.

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:05.348
No.

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:06.679
You made medical history.

00:18:06.752 --> 00:18:08.686
You won the Legate's
Crest of Valor.

00:18:08.754 --> 00:18:10.415
Awards aren't important, Doc.

00:18:10.489 --> 00:18:12.218
It's the work that matters.

00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:14.350
Of course.

00:18:14.426 --> 00:18:17.486
Still, the recognition
of your peers, your government

00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:19.087
must be very satisfying.

00:18:19.164 --> 00:18:21.530
I'm sure you've made your
share of breakthroughs.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:25.627
Naturally. Unfortunately,
no one from Starfleet

00:18:25.704 --> 00:18:27.137
ever hears about them.

00:18:27.206 --> 00:18:28.503
I toil in obscurity.

00:18:28.574 --> 00:18:31.099
Why don't you show me
your patient records?

00:18:31.176 --> 00:18:33.906
At least I'll know
about your accomplishments.

00:18:34.046 --> 00:18:35.673
All right.

00:18:35.747 --> 00:18:37.908
Everything seems to be in order.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.517
Shall we get to work?

00:18:39.585 --> 00:18:42.110
Computer, create
a holographic re-creation

00:18:42.187 --> 00:18:43.882
of the alien in Sick Bay.

00:18:45.457 --> 00:18:47.755
Hand me that cortical
stimulator, will you?

00:18:50.162 --> 00:18:51.390
Yes. Thank you.

00:18:54.433 --> 00:18:56.128
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:18:56.201 --> 00:18:58.601
While the Doctor seems
to be making progress,

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.763
Commander Chakotay and I
have hit a wall

00:19:00.839 --> 00:19:04.366
in our attempt
to decipher the alien message.

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:06.138
It was a distress call, right?

00:19:06.211 --> 00:19:08.611
So maybe if we retransmitted
that message,

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.342
others of the species would
realize we need their help.

00:19:11.416 --> 00:19:13.407
We don't know where they are.

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:15.646
We'll send it on
all subspace bands.

00:19:15.721 --> 00:19:17.120
If they're out there,
they'll hear it.

00:19:17.189 --> 00:19:18.520
They might turn out
to be unfriendly.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.750
The Doctor's pretty sure

00:19:19.825 --> 00:19:22.191
the alien is simply trying
to survive. I agree.

00:19:22.261 --> 00:19:23.751
It'll be a difficult
first contact,

00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:25.558
but we might find a way
to communicate.

00:19:25.631 --> 00:19:27.189
It's worth a shot.

00:19:28.901 --> 00:19:33.395
Tuvok, reroute auxiliary power
to the deflector dish.

00:19:33.472 --> 00:19:36.373
Retransmit the alien's message
on all subspace bands.

00:19:36.441 --> 00:19:37.703
Aye, Captain.

00:19:39.378 --> 00:19:41.243
Deflector at full capacity.

00:19:41.313 --> 00:19:44.146
Chakotay.

00:20:03.235 --> 00:20:04.167
I'm sorry.

00:20:04.236 --> 00:20:06.227
My wife tells me I'm tone deaf.

00:20:06.305 --> 00:20:07.272
Not at all.

00:20:07.339 --> 00:20:08.306
You were right on key.

00:20:08.373 --> 00:20:09.635
If you enjoy music,

00:20:09.708 --> 00:20:12.643
we can run some opera programs
after we're finished.

00:20:12.711 --> 00:20:13.905
I'd like that.

00:20:13.979 --> 00:20:16.675
I think we're ready
for a look inside.

00:20:16.748 --> 00:20:18.147
Scalpel?

00:20:20.185 --> 00:20:21.618
Forgive me for saying so,

00:20:21.687 --> 00:20:23.951
but this appears to be
a rather crude instrument,

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:26.286
especially when we have
such advanced equipment

00:20:26.358 --> 00:20:27.620
at our disposal.

00:20:27.693 --> 00:20:30.787
I often find the simplest tool
is the most effective.

00:20:30.862 --> 00:20:34.229
All of our elaborate scanners
and laser scalpels...

00:20:34.299 --> 00:20:36.494
they remove us
from our subjects.

00:20:36.568 --> 00:20:38.502
Actually feeling the anatomy,

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.800
the consistency
of the internal organs,

00:20:40.872 --> 00:20:42.533
it can be very instructive.

00:20:42.608 --> 00:20:44.701
Why don't you do the honors?

00:20:44.776 --> 00:20:49.509
Uh, make a vertical incision,
say, 12 centimeters,

00:20:49.581 --> 00:20:50.639
starting here.

00:20:55.287 --> 00:20:57.221
We're hurting it.

00:20:57.289 --> 00:20:59.382
Doctor, it's a hologram.

00:20:59.458 --> 00:21:01.255
Of course.

00:21:01.326 --> 00:21:04.261
I guess as a hologram myself,
I have a certain empathy.

00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:05.296
Keep going.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:12.869
Extraordinary.

00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:14.929
Look at that series of nodes.

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:17.338
They appear to be clustered
along the primary nerve.

00:21:17.409 --> 00:21:18.842
Multiple neocortices, I'd say.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.105
Suggesting a highly
intelligent species.

00:21:21.179 --> 00:21:23.943
Yes, but also presenting
us with a point of attack.

00:21:24.082 --> 00:21:25.106
Attack?

00:21:25.183 --> 00:21:28.175
If we induce a neurostatic shock
in one of these nodes,

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:29.948
I believe it will travel
to the others,

00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:31.817
the creature will lose
motor function

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:33.482
and we'll be able to remove it.

00:21:33.558 --> 00:21:36.049
The procedure will probably
kill the creature.

00:21:36.128 --> 00:21:37.186
Probably.

00:21:37.262 --> 00:21:39.594
I'd like to find a way
to save them both.

00:21:39.665 --> 00:21:41.428
So would I
in an ideal situation,

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.092
but we have to set priorities,

00:21:43.168 --> 00:21:45.295
which, in this case,
is your crewmate.

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:46.860
This is a sentient life-form.

00:21:46.938 --> 00:21:49.930
For all we know, it could be
this species' Einstein,

00:21:50.008 --> 00:21:50.975
its Picasso.

00:21:51.076 --> 00:21:53.135
Or he could be
a psychotic criminal.

00:21:53.211 --> 00:21:56.874
The point is, we don't know
and we have choices to make.

00:21:56.948 --> 00:21:58.848
Your program's destabilizing.

00:21:58.917 --> 00:22:00.282
This is such poor timing.

00:22:00.352 --> 00:22:03.082
I'll have to take you off-line,
but don't worry.

00:22:03.155 --> 00:22:05.589
We'll have you up
and running again in no time.

00:22:05.657 --> 00:22:08.922
Computer, take Medical
Consultant Program off-line.

00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:10.928
Doctor to Ensign Kim.

00:22:10.996 --> 00:22:11.928
Go ahead, Doc.

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:13.520
Our new program's destabilizing.

00:22:13.598 --> 00:22:14.758
I'll meet you in Sick Bay.

00:22:14.833 --> 00:22:16.733
We'll try
to reinitialize him there.

00:22:16.802 --> 00:22:18.269
Tabor, I could use some help.

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:19.361
Yes, sir.

00:22:22.074 --> 00:22:24.338
Try again.

00:22:24.409 --> 00:22:25.376
No luck.

00:22:25.444 --> 00:22:26.536
Would it be easier

00:22:26.611 --> 00:22:28.636
if we reduced
the hologram's memory load?

00:22:28.714 --> 00:22:29.908
Maybe, but I don't want

00:22:29.981 --> 00:22:32.142
to do that
unless we absolutely have to.

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:36.787
What's going on?

00:22:36.855 --> 00:22:39.483
My consultant's gone off-line.

00:22:39.558 --> 00:22:40.923
The Cardassian?

00:22:40.992 --> 00:22:43.085
You can leave him off.

00:22:43.161 --> 00:22:45.857
I'm surprised
by your attitude, Lieutenant.

00:22:45.931 --> 00:22:48.126
I never took you for someone

00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:51.067
who would make generalizations
based on race.

00:22:51.136 --> 00:22:55.835
When it comes to Cardassians,
I'm guilty as charged.

00:22:55.907 --> 00:23:00.435
I understand your experience
with them was unpleasant,

00:23:00.512 --> 00:23:02.742
but if you give Crell a chance,
I think you'll find

00:23:02.814 --> 00:23:05.146
that he's a friendly,
compassionate man,

00:23:05.217 --> 00:23:07.242
not to mention a genius
who's trying to save your life.

00:23:07.319 --> 00:23:11.187
I'll skip the introductions
if it's all the same to you.

00:23:11.256 --> 00:23:12.848
Suit yourself,

00:23:12.924 --> 00:23:16.121
but you should know
I plan on asking the Captain

00:23:16.194 --> 00:23:18.924
to keep him on
as a permanent consultant.

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:22.625
I'm not the only one who's going
to have a problem with that.

00:23:22.701 --> 00:23:24.931
Well, you'll just have
to get used to it.

00:23:25.003 --> 00:23:27.597
Who knows?
You may even grow to like him.

00:23:27.672 --> 00:23:30.163
Don't hold your breath.

00:23:32.677 --> 00:23:34.076
How's it coming?

00:23:34.146 --> 00:23:35.135
We're close.

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:37.147
Actually,
I think that should do it.

00:23:37.215 --> 00:23:38.648
Good.

00:23:38.717 --> 00:23:40.150
Computer, reactivate

00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:42.709
Medical Consultant Program
Beta-1.

00:23:45.257 --> 00:23:46.315
Hello, again.

00:23:46.391 --> 00:23:48.154
My God.

00:23:48.226 --> 00:23:49.386
What's wrong?

00:23:49.461 --> 00:23:51.224
That's Crell Moset.

00:23:51.296 --> 00:23:53.355
Yes. Do I know you?

00:23:53.432 --> 00:23:56.799
He killed my brother,
my grandfather...

00:23:56.868 --> 00:23:58.699
hundreds of people.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:01.136
He's a mass murderer.

00:24:08.146 --> 00:24:09.135
You must be mistaken.

00:24:09.214 --> 00:24:11.045
It's no mistake.

00:24:11.116 --> 00:24:13.107
Moset performed experiments
on living people.

00:24:13.185 --> 00:24:14.584
Thousands of Bajorans
were killed

00:24:14.653 --> 00:24:16.018
in his so-called hospital.

00:24:16.087 --> 00:24:17.019
Is this true?

00:24:17.088 --> 00:24:18.248
No, no. He's...

00:24:18.323 --> 00:24:20.450
There must be
some misunderstanding.

00:24:20.525 --> 00:24:21.514
The liar.

00:24:21.593 --> 00:24:23.026
Take it easy, Tabor.

00:24:23.094 --> 00:24:24.721
Whoa. He's just a hologram.

00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:26.127
I'm upsetting him.

00:24:26.198 --> 00:24:27.130
I should go.

00:24:27.199 --> 00:24:28.632
I'm sorry about this.

00:24:30.235 --> 00:24:33.102
Computer, transfer
Medical Consultant Program

00:24:33.171 --> 00:24:34.502
to Holodeck 2.

00:24:41.012 --> 00:24:45.676
I can still remember the sounds
his instruments made...

00:24:45.750 --> 00:24:48.776
the screams of his patients...

00:24:48.854 --> 00:24:49.821
the smell...

00:24:49.888 --> 00:24:52.083
of chemicals and dead flesh.

00:24:54.159 --> 00:24:56.650
He operated on my grandfather...

00:24:56.728 --> 00:25:00.289
exposed his internal organs
to nadion radiation.

00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:02.458
It took six days for him to die.

00:25:02.534 --> 00:25:05.867
I promised myself
I would never forget.

00:25:05.937 --> 00:25:07.302
You were very young.

00:25:07.372 --> 00:25:10.864
Is it possible your memory
of these events is inaccurate?

00:25:10.942 --> 00:25:12.273
My memory's just fine.

00:25:12.344 --> 00:25:15.006
He blinded people so he
could study how they adapted,

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:17.344
exposed them to polytrinic
acid just to see

00:25:17.415 --> 00:25:19.849
how long it would take
for their skin to heal.

00:25:19.918 --> 00:25:22.716
Ensign, the man you're accusing
cured the Fostossa virus.

00:25:22.787 --> 00:25:25.517
He stopped an epidemic that
killed thousands of Bajorans.

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:27.353
By infecting hundreds
of people...

00:25:27.425 --> 00:25:30.258
so that he could experiment
with different treatments...

00:25:30.328 --> 00:25:31.795
old, helpless people...

00:25:31.863 --> 00:25:33.592
like my grandfather...

00:25:33.665 --> 00:25:35.929
because he considered
their lives worthless.

00:25:36.001 --> 00:25:37.366
How do you know this?

00:25:37.435 --> 00:25:38.697
Everybody knew.

00:25:38.770 --> 00:25:41.466
I remember some of the Maquis
under my command

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:44.202
talking about an infamous
Cardassian doctor.

00:25:45.944 --> 00:25:48.139
Could these simply
have been rumors

00:25:48.213 --> 00:25:50.943
spread by Bajorans
who hated the Cardassians?

00:25:51.082 --> 00:25:52.106
I was there.

00:25:53.451 --> 00:25:57.251
I don't understand
why this isn't in our database.

00:25:57.322 --> 00:25:59.654
The Cardassians
didn't exactly publicize

00:25:59.724 --> 00:26:01.749
their wartime medical practices.

00:26:01.826 --> 00:26:04.624
I wouldn't be surprised
if the real Moset went on

00:26:04.696 --> 00:26:06.027
to live a normal life.

00:26:06.097 --> 00:26:10.534
He's the Chairman of Exobiology
at the University of Culat.

00:26:12.103 --> 00:26:14.162
We may not be able
to do anything

00:26:14.239 --> 00:26:16.503
about the real Moset,
Commander...

00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:19.203
but the program
should be destroyed.

00:26:19.277 --> 00:26:21.245
Every trace
of that man's research

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:23.247
should be deleted
from the database.

00:26:25.884 --> 00:26:28.148
I had a bad feeling
about that hologram

00:26:28.219 --> 00:26:29.481
the second I saw him.

00:26:29.554 --> 00:26:31.954
Looks like your instinct
was right.

00:26:33.458 --> 00:26:35.050
I won't let him near me.

00:26:35.126 --> 00:26:37.617
You're kidding, right?

00:26:37.696 --> 00:26:40.130
No, I am dead serious.

00:26:40.198 --> 00:26:41.790
B'Elanna...

00:26:41.866 --> 00:26:44.164
If I let that pig
operate on me...

00:26:44.235 --> 00:26:48.103
I'll be benefiting
from other people's suffering.

00:26:48.173 --> 00:26:49.800
You're not being rational.

00:26:49.874 --> 00:26:52.240
I won't do it.

00:26:54.479 --> 00:26:56.310
What's happening?

00:26:56.381 --> 00:26:59.077
Her cytotoxin levels are
going through the roof.

00:26:59.150 --> 00:27:00.617
Pulse is rapid and irregular.

00:27:00.685 --> 00:27:03.176
No doubt you've said
something to upset her.

00:27:03.254 --> 00:27:07.020
What she's upset about, Doc,
is your Cardassian buddy.

00:27:07.092 --> 00:27:08.024
Tell him.

00:27:08.093 --> 00:27:09.355
Tell me what?

00:27:09.427 --> 00:27:11.588
She refuses
to let him treat her.

00:27:11.663 --> 00:27:13.893
B'Elanna, we're very close
to a solution.

00:27:14.032 --> 00:27:15.090
Do it...

00:27:15.166 --> 00:27:16.531
...without him.

00:27:16.601 --> 00:27:18.694
I don't know that I can.

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:19.998
Find another way.

00:27:22.807 --> 00:27:24.536
She's going
into cytotoxic shock!

00:27:24.609 --> 00:27:26.668
Two milligrams inaprovaline!

00:27:35.887 --> 00:27:38.287
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:27:38.356 --> 00:27:41.120
I've managed to stabilize
Lieutenant Torres

00:27:41.192 --> 00:27:44.093
for the time being,
but the matter of how to proceed

00:27:44.162 --> 00:27:46.562
with her treatment
remains unresolved.

00:27:46.631 --> 00:27:48.394
Isolate data block 0459.

00:27:48.466 --> 00:27:49.763
Ensign.

00:27:49.834 --> 00:27:50.823
You wanted to see me?

00:27:50.902 --> 00:27:52.369
We've been looking for evidence

00:27:52.437 --> 00:27:54.132
that might support
Tabor's accusations.

00:27:54.205 --> 00:27:55.263
Anything?

00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:56.705
Actually, that's
why we called you here.

00:27:56.775 --> 00:27:57.707
It's not looking good.

00:27:57.776 --> 00:27:58.708
Show me.

00:27:58.777 --> 00:27:59.835
We've been reviewing data

00:27:59.911 --> 00:28:01.572
on the Cardassian
occupation of Bajor...

00:28:01.646 --> 00:28:03.580
the alleged site
of Moset's crimes.

00:28:03.648 --> 00:28:06.242
Strategic information,
log entries kept in battle,

00:28:06.317 --> 00:28:09.252
sensor scans from Starfleet
vessels... this, for example.

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:12.517
Requisition records from one
of Crell Moset's hospitals.

00:28:12.590 --> 00:28:14.080
He was purchasing
biochemical agents,

00:28:14.159 --> 00:28:16.457
including every known strain
of the Fostossa virus.

00:28:16.528 --> 00:28:18.723
Of course he needed
samples of the virus.

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:20.628
That's how vaccines
are developed.

00:28:20.699 --> 00:28:22.394
Take a look
at the requisition orders.

00:28:24.602 --> 00:28:26.695
Moset didn't ask
for any of the enzymes

00:28:26.771 --> 00:28:29.205
normally required
for synthesizing a vaccine.

00:28:29.274 --> 00:28:30.536
It gets worse.

00:28:30.608 --> 00:28:33.008
Four days after he received
the virus samples,

00:28:33.078 --> 00:28:35.103
there was a minor outbreak
of Fostossa

00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:36.875
in the vicinity of his hospital.

00:28:36.948 --> 00:28:38.279
Prior to that date,

00:28:38.349 --> 00:28:41.910
there had not been a single case
in the entire province.

00:28:41.986 --> 00:28:45.422
I have to report these findings
to Commander Chakotay.

00:28:47.792 --> 00:28:48.918
It is curious.

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:52.655
The Borg are accused
of assimilating information

00:28:52.731 --> 00:28:54.528
with no regard for life.

00:28:54.599 --> 00:28:56.658
This Cardassian did the same

00:28:56.735 --> 00:28:59.363
and yet, his behavior
is tolerated.

00:29:11.916 --> 00:29:13.281
Ah, there you are.

00:29:13.351 --> 00:29:16.013
I'm almost ready
to begin the surgery.

00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:18.783
Lieutenant Torres won't allow
you to have anything to do

00:29:18.857 --> 00:29:20.654
with her treatment.

00:29:20.725 --> 00:29:23.023
Because of that Bajoran?

00:29:23.094 --> 00:29:25.858
We've gathered
some corroborating evidence.

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:28.364
It appears that he's
telling the truth.

00:29:28.433 --> 00:29:30.663
You committed
a series of atrocities

00:29:30.735 --> 00:29:32.362
during the Cardassian War.

00:29:32.437 --> 00:29:35.873
Thousands of Bajorans died
on your surgical tables.

00:29:35.940 --> 00:29:37.100
That's absurd.

00:29:37.175 --> 00:29:40.406
And even if it were true,
I'm only a hologram

00:29:40.478 --> 00:29:43.140
and I have no memory
of those events.

00:29:43.214 --> 00:29:45.705
They're not part
of my programming.

00:29:45.784 --> 00:29:50.380
But you are the holographic
representation of Crell Moset.

00:29:50.455 --> 00:29:54.289
Your program,
despite all its brilliance,

00:29:54.359 --> 00:29:56.384
is based on his work.

00:29:56.461 --> 00:29:58.395
He infected patients,

00:29:58.463 --> 00:30:02.126
exposed them to polytrinic acid,
mutilated their living bodies

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:05.533
and now we're reaping the
benefits of those experiments.

00:30:05.603 --> 00:30:09.903
Medically, ethically,
it's wrong.

00:30:09.974 --> 00:30:12.738
What do you suggest
we do about it?

00:30:12.811 --> 00:30:15.405
I'm not sure.

00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:18.244
We may have
to delete your program.

00:30:18.316 --> 00:30:19.578
Delete me?

00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:21.585
What about our patient?

00:30:21.653 --> 00:30:24.918
I suppose I'd have to try
and treat her on my own.

00:30:24.989 --> 00:30:28.925
No offense, but you need me.

00:30:28.993 --> 00:30:29.960
I realize that.

00:30:30.094 --> 00:30:31.425
You're a physician.

00:30:31.496 --> 00:30:34.158
You know there's always
a price to pay

00:30:34.232 --> 00:30:36.962
for the advancement
of medical science.

00:30:37.068 --> 00:30:38.933
Sometimes that price
is too high.

00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:40.163
Torture?

00:30:40.238 --> 00:30:42.206
Your word, not mine.

00:30:42.273 --> 00:30:45.936
I cured the Fostossa virus,
didn't I?

00:30:46.010 --> 00:30:48.205
So these experiments
you say I conducted

00:30:48.279 --> 00:30:50.440
obviously helped me
devise a treatment.

00:30:50.515 --> 00:30:52.881
Imagine how many lives
would have been lost

00:30:52.951 --> 00:30:54.942
if I hadn't eliminated
this disease.

00:30:55.019 --> 00:30:56.247
That doesn't justify

00:30:56.321 --> 00:30:58.755
using people
in laboratory experiments.

00:30:58.823 --> 00:31:00.791
As I explained to you,

00:31:00.859 --> 00:31:05.489
during the occupation,
I was forced to improvise.

00:31:05.563 --> 00:31:08.225
I used what resources I had.

00:31:08.299 --> 00:31:11.427
And ethical considerations,
they mean nothing to you?

00:31:11.502 --> 00:31:14.903
Ethics are arbitrary.

00:31:14.973 --> 00:31:21.071
How do you suppose your own
database was developed? Hmm?

00:31:21.145 --> 00:31:24.740
My God, half the medical
knowledge acquired on Earth

00:31:24.816 --> 00:31:27.717
came through experiments
on lower animals.

00:31:27.785 --> 00:31:29.446
But not people.

00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:31.283
It's convenient to draw a line

00:31:31.356 --> 00:31:33.950
between higher and lower
species, isn't it?

00:31:34.058 --> 00:31:36.151
This is the 24th century, Crell.

00:31:36.227 --> 00:31:39.128
Your kind of barbarism
ended a long time ago

00:31:39.197 --> 00:31:41.131
or, at least, it should have.

00:31:41.199 --> 00:31:43.167
What difference does it make

00:31:43.234 --> 00:31:45.725
how long ago
the research occurred?

00:31:45.803 --> 00:31:48.237
What matters is
that we can use it

00:31:48.306 --> 00:31:49.967
to help patients today.

00:31:50.074 --> 00:31:53.339
Now, are you going

00:31:53.411 --> 00:31:59.975
to delete my program and all
of the research it contains,

00:32:00.118 --> 00:32:04.851
or are we going to use it
to save B'Elanna's life?

00:32:11.462 --> 00:32:13.123
Come in.

00:32:13.197 --> 00:32:15.290
Commander.

00:32:17.168 --> 00:32:20.660
This request of yours
to be relieved of duty...

00:32:20.738 --> 00:32:22.035
I won't grant it.

00:32:22.106 --> 00:32:24.233
I have the right
to resign my commission.

00:32:24.309 --> 00:32:25.469
For what reason?

00:32:25.543 --> 00:32:28.011
Moral objections
to this ship's medical policy.

00:32:30.982 --> 00:32:33.849
I understand
how difficult this is for you,

00:32:33.918 --> 00:32:35.886
but you've got
to let go of the past.

00:32:35.954 --> 00:32:38.946
Focus on today, and today,
B'Elanna's life is in danger.

00:32:39.090 --> 00:32:40.955
Everything else
should be put aside.

00:32:41.092 --> 00:32:41.956
You don't have the right

00:32:42.093 --> 00:32:43.287
to violate the memory
of my family.

00:32:43.361 --> 00:32:45.522
As long as that Cardassian
hologram is on line,

00:32:45.596 --> 00:32:47.154
that's exactly
what you're doing.

00:32:47.231 --> 00:32:48.630
It's not that simple.

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:49.962
It is to me.

00:32:50.101 --> 00:32:53.127
Crell Moset killed thousands
of people in his hospitals.

00:32:53.204 --> 00:32:56.105
As long as we're willing
to benefit from his research,

00:32:56.174 --> 00:32:57.698
we're no better than he is.

00:33:02.714 --> 00:33:04.011
If I had weeks, or even days,

00:33:04.082 --> 00:33:06.016
maybe I could come up
with an alternative,

00:33:06.084 --> 00:33:08.678
but time is of the essence
and Moset's idea will work.

00:33:08.753 --> 00:33:10.220
Then you've got to use it.

00:33:10.288 --> 00:33:12.415
Even if the Doctor
could perform the surgery

00:33:12.490 --> 00:33:13.514
without Moset's help,

00:33:13.591 --> 00:33:15.491
he'd still be using
the man's research.

00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:17.755
That would be going
against B'Elanna's wishes.

00:33:17.829 --> 00:33:19.126
We're talking about a woman

00:33:19.197 --> 00:33:21.722
who has alien tendrils
sapping the life out of her.

00:33:21.799 --> 00:33:23.664
She's obviously
not thinking straight.

00:33:23.735 --> 00:33:24.667
On the contrary.

00:33:24.736 --> 00:33:26.328
Her concerns are based in logic.

00:33:26.404 --> 00:33:28.167
Logic?

00:33:28.239 --> 00:33:30.298
If the Doctor uses knowledge
that Moset gained

00:33:30.375 --> 00:33:32.536
through his experiments,
we would be validating

00:33:32.610 --> 00:33:35.101
his methods, inviting
further unethical research.

00:33:35.179 --> 00:33:36.771
We'd be setting
a terrible precedent.

00:33:36.848 --> 00:33:39.043
We're in the middle
of the Delta Quadrant.

00:33:39.117 --> 00:33:40.049
Who would know?

00:33:40.118 --> 00:33:41.517
We would know.

00:33:41.586 --> 00:33:42.644
Fine.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:44.654
Let's just deactivate
the evil hologram

00:33:44.722 --> 00:33:45.814
and let B'Elanna die.

00:33:45.890 --> 00:33:47.915
At least, we'd have
our morals intact.

00:33:47.992 --> 00:33:49.823
- Tom.
- And you, Chakotay,

00:33:49.894 --> 00:33:51.885
since when do you care
what Starfleet thinks?

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:53.658
This isn't about rules
and regulations.

00:33:53.731 --> 00:33:55.198
This is about doing
what's right.

00:33:55.266 --> 00:33:56.733
Spoken like a true Maquis.

00:33:56.801 --> 00:33:58.462
Well, if you'd just
set aside your hatred

00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:00.470
of the Cardassian
for one second...

00:34:00.538 --> 00:34:01.470
Enough, Lieutenant.

00:34:01.539 --> 00:34:02.904
All right, all right.

00:34:02.974 --> 00:34:05.636
The arguments have been made
and we're running out of time.

00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:07.075
The fact is, you're both right.

00:34:07.145 --> 00:34:08.407
But when it comes down to it,

00:34:08.479 --> 00:34:09.912
the only issue
I'm concerned about

00:34:10.048 --> 00:34:12.482
is the well-being of that
crew member lying in Sick Bay.

00:34:12.550 --> 00:34:15.314
We'll wrestle with the morality
of this situation later...

00:34:15.386 --> 00:34:17.217
after B'Elanna is
back on her feet.

00:34:17.288 --> 00:34:19.916
Doctor, you have
my authorization to proceed

00:34:20.058 --> 00:34:21.548
with Moset's assistance.

00:34:21.626 --> 00:34:22.718
Yes, Captain.

00:34:22.794 --> 00:34:25.092
Any consequences
of this decision

00:34:25.163 --> 00:34:27.063
will be my responsibility.

00:34:27.131 --> 00:34:30.191
Dismissed.

00:34:38.976 --> 00:34:40.603
Thanks.

00:34:53.424 --> 00:34:55.585
Scalpel.

00:35:07.972 --> 00:35:11.339
Ensign Kim,
do you hear something?

00:35:11.409 --> 00:35:12.899
Hear what?

00:35:12.977 --> 00:35:14.911
A series of high frequencies.

00:35:15.046 --> 00:35:16.775
They are getting louder.

00:35:16.848 --> 00:35:18.907
Must be those Vulcan
ears of yours.

00:35:20.818 --> 00:35:22.012
I hear it, too.

00:35:22.086 --> 00:35:23.644
Anything on sensors?

00:35:24.922 --> 00:35:27.482
It appears to be
an alien com signal.

00:35:27.558 --> 00:35:28.718
Triaxilating wavelengths.

00:35:28.793 --> 00:35:29.725
Origins?

00:35:29.794 --> 00:35:30.886
Unknown.

00:35:32.163 --> 00:35:34.131
Captain, a vessel
just dropped out of warp.

00:35:34.198 --> 00:35:35.631
Approaching fast
off the port bow.

00:35:35.700 --> 00:35:36.792
On screen.

00:35:38.035 --> 00:35:40.196
Can we dampen it a little?

00:35:40.271 --> 00:35:41.238
Negative.

00:35:43.074 --> 00:35:47.033
Harry, tell me that was just
their way of saying hello.

00:35:47.111 --> 00:35:48.237
I wish I could.

00:35:48.312 --> 00:35:51.406
The universal translator
doesn't have a clue.

00:35:51.482 --> 00:35:53.313
Perhaps they are waiting
for our response.

00:35:53.384 --> 00:35:55.944
Well, then, let's give them one.

00:35:56.087 --> 00:35:59.614
Open a channel,
all subspace bands.

00:36:00.725 --> 00:36:02.056
This is Captain Janeway

00:36:02.126 --> 00:36:04.185
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:36:04.262 --> 00:36:06.321
We cannot interpret
your message,

00:36:06.397 --> 00:36:08.194
but please try to understand,

00:36:08.266 --> 00:36:12.134
we are on a peaceful mission
and we intend you no harm.

00:36:12.203 --> 00:36:15.661
We have one of your kind
on board our ship.

00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:19.005
It's injured and we're
attempting to provide treatment.

00:36:19.076 --> 00:36:20.771
If you can understand...

00:36:22.380 --> 00:36:27.317
I'm ready to stimulate
the primary neural pathways.

00:36:27.385 --> 00:36:29.683
Cortical probe.

00:36:32.823 --> 00:36:36.224
I'm applying it
to the primary neocortex.

00:36:37.728 --> 00:36:40.458
Its motor control is weakening,

00:36:40.531 --> 00:36:44.092
but not enough
to release the patient.

00:36:44.168 --> 00:36:47.797
Our little friend
needs a bigger jolt.

00:36:47.872 --> 00:36:50.898
I'm increasing
the pulse frequency...

00:36:52.276 --> 00:36:53.675
The synapses are degenerating.

00:36:53.744 --> 00:36:54.733
You're killing it.

00:36:54.812 --> 00:36:56.507
Don't lose your nerve, Doctor...

00:36:56.581 --> 00:36:57.946
not when we're this close.

00:36:58.049 --> 00:36:59.482
Lower the pulse frequency.

00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:02.212
If I do that, the creature
will regain control.

00:37:02.286 --> 00:37:03.218
I don't care.
Lower the pulse.

00:37:03.287 --> 00:37:04.982
- Doctor...
- Lower the pulse frequency

00:37:05.056 --> 00:37:06.819
or I'll take
your program off-line.

00:37:08.893 --> 00:37:11.885
You realize you're reducing
our chances of saving her?

00:37:11.963 --> 00:37:13.225
Not necessarily.

00:37:13.297 --> 00:37:14.594
Give me the probe.

00:37:14.665 --> 00:37:16.098
The probe, Doctor.

00:37:19.370 --> 00:37:21.861
If we apply the pulse
to the secondary neocortex,

00:37:21.939 --> 00:37:24.305
we should be able
to achieve the same results

00:37:24.375 --> 00:37:25.467
at a lower frequency.

00:37:25.543 --> 00:37:27.636
Not particularly efficient.

00:37:29.447 --> 00:37:32.416
But it might prove interesting.

00:37:32.483 --> 00:37:35.611
I'm reading an energy surge
in their forward section.

00:37:35.686 --> 00:37:38.052
Shields!

00:37:44.128 --> 00:37:46.596
Doctor to Bridge.
The holodeck's going off-line.

00:37:46.664 --> 00:37:47.790
What's happening up there?

00:37:47.865 --> 00:37:48.854
Stand by, Doctor.

00:37:48.933 --> 00:37:51.197
They've locked on to us
with some sort of tractor beam.

00:37:51.269 --> 00:37:52.531
It's draining our power.

00:37:52.603 --> 00:37:54.730
Reroute emergency power
to the holodeck.

00:37:54.805 --> 00:37:57.569
Send an antimatter surge
through the shield matrix.

00:37:57.642 --> 00:37:59.303
See if that'll
loosen their grip.

00:38:00.478 --> 00:38:02.036
No effect.

00:38:02.113 --> 00:38:04.445
We do have weapons.

00:38:04.515 --> 00:38:05.607
No. If they wanted
to destroy us,

00:38:05.683 --> 00:38:07.014
they wouldn't be using
a tractor beam.

00:38:07.084 --> 00:38:08.517
They're trying to rescue
their crew member.

00:38:08.586 --> 00:38:09.883
Captain...

00:38:10.021 --> 00:38:12.080
This isn't about logic, Tuvok,
it's about instinct.

00:38:12.156 --> 00:38:13.589
Now, I may not speak
their language,

00:38:13.658 --> 00:38:14.682
but I have a gut feeling

00:38:14.759 --> 00:38:16.886
they don't want an armed
conflict any more than we do.

00:38:16.994 --> 00:38:18.086
Bridge to Doctor.

00:38:18.162 --> 00:38:19.094
What's your status?

00:38:19.163 --> 00:38:20.323
The procedure's working.

00:38:20.398 --> 00:38:21.524
Almost there, Captain.

00:38:21.599 --> 00:38:22.861
It's losing motor control.

00:38:22.933 --> 00:38:24.332
The tendrils are withdrawing

00:38:24.402 --> 00:38:26.097
from her lungs,
liver, kidneys...

00:38:29.006 --> 00:38:30.906
The alien's life signs
are failing.

00:38:30.975 --> 00:38:32.670
We need a substitute
for the metabolic energy

00:38:32.743 --> 00:38:33.835
it was taking from B'Elanna.

00:38:33.911 --> 00:38:36.573
Could we restore
its own metabolism?

00:38:36.647 --> 00:38:38.842
Perhaps. Give it
40 milligrams of stenophyl.

00:38:38.916 --> 00:38:41.851
It's going
into anaphylactic shock.

00:38:41.919 --> 00:38:42.908
All right.

00:38:42.987 --> 00:38:45.353
Increasing the dosage
to 60 milligrams...

00:38:45.423 --> 00:38:47.220
We've lost power
on Decks 7 through 12.

00:38:47.291 --> 00:38:48.519
Shields are failing, Captain.

00:38:48.592 --> 00:38:49.524
Doctor?

00:38:49.593 --> 00:38:50.787
Stand by, Captain.

00:38:50.861 --> 00:38:52.158
Anaphylaxia is subsiding.

00:38:52.229 --> 00:38:54.527
Its electrolytic reactions
are increasing.

00:38:54.598 --> 00:38:56.862
Its metabolism is
stabilizing on its own.

00:38:56.934 --> 00:38:58.959
Bridge, beam the life-form
to its ship.

00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:04.403
Transport complete.

00:39:05.443 --> 00:39:07.968
The alien ship is
withdrawing, Captain.

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:14.979
You're welcome.

00:39:21.559 --> 00:39:23.857
I've released B'Elanna
to her quarters.

00:39:23.928 --> 00:39:25.418
Her condition?

00:39:25.496 --> 00:39:28.431
Stable, but her nervous system
has suffered extreme trauma.

00:39:28.499 --> 00:39:31.161
She'll need time to recover...
several days, at least.

00:39:31.235 --> 00:39:32.759
Good work.

00:39:32.837 --> 00:39:34.668
I should caution you, Captain...

00:39:34.739 --> 00:39:37.469
when I told her
that we'd used Moset's program,

00:39:37.541 --> 00:39:39.532
she was unhappy,
to put it mildly.

00:39:39.610 --> 00:39:41.237
I nearly had to sedate her.

00:39:41.312 --> 00:39:44.475
It sounds like her Klingon
temper has fully recovered.

00:39:44.548 --> 00:39:47.415
It practically qualifies
as a chronic condition.

00:39:47.485 --> 00:39:49.919
I'll speak to her.

00:39:49.987 --> 00:39:51.716
There's one more topic
of concern.

00:39:51.789 --> 00:39:53.518
Should we delete the program

00:39:53.591 --> 00:39:56.890
or keep Moset in our database
for future emergencies?

00:39:58.996 --> 00:40:01.624
I'm inclined to leave
this up to you, Doctor.

00:40:01.699 --> 00:40:04.395
You are the Chief Medical
Officer on this ship.

00:40:04.468 --> 00:40:06.561
As far as I'm concerned,
there's no one

00:40:06.637 --> 00:40:09.105
more qualified than you
to make that decision.

00:40:09.173 --> 00:40:10.105
Thank you, Captain.

00:40:10.174 --> 00:40:11.436
But please make it quickly.

00:40:11.509 --> 00:40:13.033
I'm eager to resolve
this matter.

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:14.839
There's been enough
moral controversy

00:40:14.912 --> 00:40:16.140
on this ship for one day.

00:40:22.086 --> 00:40:23.110
Come in.

00:40:26.624 --> 00:40:28.057
At ease.

00:40:29.627 --> 00:40:30.958
Interesting fragrance.

00:40:31.028 --> 00:40:34.486
I'm surprised it hasn't set off
the environmental alarms.

00:40:34.565 --> 00:40:37.329
It's a combination
of mental relaxant

00:40:37.401 --> 00:40:39.164
and expeller of demons.

00:40:39.236 --> 00:40:41.670
It's an ancient Klingon remedy.

00:40:41.739 --> 00:40:43.969
Feeling any better?

00:40:44.074 --> 00:40:45.974
I'm alive.

00:40:46.076 --> 00:40:47.976
I hope you can understand

00:40:48.045 --> 00:40:51.139
why I went against
your wishes, B'Elanna.

00:40:51.215 --> 00:40:53.274
Losing you was unacceptable.

00:40:56.086 --> 00:40:58.953
I know you're angry, but we
need to put this behind us.

00:40:59.023 --> 00:41:00.081
Understood?

00:41:00.157 --> 00:41:01.317
Is that an order?

00:41:01.392 --> 00:41:02.825
Yes.

00:41:02.893 --> 00:41:05.589
You can't order someone to get
rid of an emotion, Captain.

00:41:05.663 --> 00:41:07.255
And what emotion is that?

00:41:07.331 --> 00:41:10.858
You had no right
to make that decision for me!

00:41:10.935 --> 00:41:12.562
I'm the Captain.

00:41:12.636 --> 00:41:14.467
You're my crewman.

00:41:14.538 --> 00:41:17.302
I did what I thought best.

00:41:19.577 --> 00:41:23.843
I get the feeling there are
still a few demons in the air.

00:41:23.914 --> 00:41:26.508
Let's hope this does
the trick, hmm?

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:41.965
Doc...

00:41:42.032 --> 00:41:43.397
how's our patient?

00:41:43.467 --> 00:41:44.491
Recuperating.

00:41:44.568 --> 00:41:46.661
We did it.

00:41:46.737 --> 00:41:48.967
Yes... we did.

00:41:49.106 --> 00:41:52.303
A celebration is in order.

00:41:52.376 --> 00:41:57.837
How about listening to that
opera you promised me?

00:41:57.915 --> 00:41:59.439
Oh, you're, uh...

00:41:59.517 --> 00:42:03.715
still wrestling with
your ethical subroutines.

00:42:03.787 --> 00:42:05.254
Take my advice.

00:42:05.322 --> 00:42:07.313
It's a waste of time.

00:42:07.391 --> 00:42:11.384
What's important is that
we saved two lives today.

00:42:11.462 --> 00:42:13.930
I'm not concerned with today.

00:42:14.064 --> 00:42:16.931
It's tomorrow I'm worried about.

00:42:17.001 --> 00:42:20.095
Captain Janeway has left
your future in my hands.

00:42:20.170 --> 00:42:21.194
She believes that,

00:42:21.272 --> 00:42:23.297
as Voyager's
Chief Medical Officer,

00:42:23.374 --> 00:42:24.932
it's up to me to decide

00:42:25.042 --> 00:42:28.205
whether your program
remains in our database.

00:42:28.279 --> 00:42:34.081
Personally, I predict a long
and fruitful collaboration

00:42:34.151 --> 00:42:35.209
between us.

00:42:35.286 --> 00:42:36.548
Oh?

00:42:36.620 --> 00:42:41.580
Think about what we accomplished
in the last 24 hours.

00:42:41.659 --> 00:42:44.389
Our first case was a triumph.

00:42:44.461 --> 00:42:46.725
Both patients are thriving

00:42:46.797 --> 00:42:51.063
and we advanced the frontiers
of medical science.

00:42:51.135 --> 00:42:53.729
I've already outlined a paper

00:42:53.804 --> 00:42:56.830
that you and I
will one day present

00:42:56.907 --> 00:42:59.398
to the Federation
Medical Academy:

00:42:59.476 --> 00:43:04.311
"Total Systemic Invasion
of a Klingon-human Hybrid

00:43:04.381 --> 00:43:07.350
By a Cytoplasmic
Pseudo-parasite."

00:43:07.418 --> 00:43:10.410
Has a nice ring to it,
don't you think?

00:43:11.822 --> 00:43:13.517
Are we also going to tell them

00:43:13.591 --> 00:43:15.889
where you honed
your surgical techniques?

00:43:15.960 --> 00:43:17.894
A footnote, perhaps...

00:43:17.962 --> 00:43:22.399
"For further details,
see Cardassian death camps."

00:43:22.466 --> 00:43:24.661
Those techniques
were crucial this morning.

00:43:24.735 --> 00:43:26.100
Where was your sarcasm then?

00:43:26.170 --> 00:43:29.230
I didn't come here to debate
the issue with you, Crell.

00:43:29.306 --> 00:43:32.935
I came here to inform you
of my decision.

00:43:33.077 --> 00:43:36.843
"It is my judgment that
the Medical Consultant Program

00:43:36.914 --> 00:43:39.747
"and all the algorithms
contained therein

00:43:39.817 --> 00:43:42.308
"shall be deleted
from the database.

00:43:42.386 --> 00:43:45.253
"In light of recent evidence,

00:43:45.322 --> 00:43:48.485
"I cannot in good conscience
utilize research

00:43:48.559 --> 00:43:52.552
that was derived
from such inhuman practices."

00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:55.190
"In good conscience"?

00:43:55.265 --> 00:43:57.563
What about the well-being
of your crew?

00:43:57.635 --> 00:44:00.661
You're confronted by
new forms of life every day...

00:44:00.738 --> 00:44:02.137
many of them dangerous.

00:44:02.206 --> 00:44:04.197
You need me.

00:44:04.274 --> 00:44:05.639
Delete my program

00:44:05.709 --> 00:44:09.907
and you violate the first oath
you took as a physician:

00:44:10.047 --> 00:44:12.880
"Do no harm."

00:44:12.950 --> 00:44:17.819
"Do no harm..." you have
no right to say those words.

00:44:17.888 --> 00:44:19.515
Computer...

00:44:19.590 --> 00:44:21.558
You can erase my program,
Doctor,

00:44:21.625 --> 00:44:23.650
but you can never
change the fact

00:44:23.727 --> 00:44:26.890
that you've already used
some of my research.

00:44:28.399 --> 00:44:32.335
Where was your conscience
when B'Elanna was dying

00:44:32.403 --> 00:44:34.928
on that table?

00:44:35.072 --> 00:44:38.098
Ethics? Morality?

00:44:38.175 --> 00:44:39.938
Conscience?

00:44:40.077 --> 00:44:42.910
Funny how they all go
out the airlock

00:44:42.980 --> 00:44:44.845
when we need something.

00:44:48.752 --> 00:44:51.949
Are you and I
really so different?

00:44:55.459 --> 00:44:59.896
Computer, delete
Medical Consultant Program

00:44:59.963 --> 00:45:01.760
and all related files.
